# Railcar GLB preserves component damage and disposes cleanly

The E2 armored railcar presentation now uses the merged three-mesh `railcar.glb` on full and balanced performance tiers. Effective LITE tier and GLB load failure retain the painted component billboards.

Runtime validates the three named meshes, three named morph targets, shared source material, and 10,948-triangle contract before mounting. Each runtime mesh gets a material clone so the wheels, boiler, and cabin can show independent damage cues at the existing `<=50% HP` threshold.

Destroyed component IDs persist while sibling components live, including when death happens before the asynchronous GLB load completes. Missing components reconstructed from suspend state are treated as destroyed. The GLB is disposed on last-component death, pool clear, run/wave reset, and pool disposal; correlated desktop and mobile probes both observed `-3` geometries and `-4` textures after pure despawn.

The boss HP bar must use the GLB's authored 1.202-unit height and scale `1`, not the old billboard `visualScale`. Independent visual review accepted the compact bar placement and the three full-frame damage cues after the wheels cue was strengthened.

Related: [[Armored Railcar damage reads before defeat — 2026-07-14 0658]] · [[Gold Rush MOC]] · [[Sessions/codex/2026-07-14-wire-railcar-3d]]

